    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 22 tests pass with BUILD SUCCESS. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` on owner creation \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same firstName and lastName, compared case-insensitively.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `AssignCustomerCode`/`AssignHouseholdId` steps), the changes were:\n\n1. **New function** `AssignNamesakeCount.java` \u2014 takes the built `@Val Owner` and the `OwnerRepository`, counts existing owners whose trimmed/lower-cased firstName **and** lastName match, and sets `owner.setNamesakeCount(count)`. Runs before `save`, so the count excludes the not-yet-persisted owner.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** in `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `assignNamesakeCount` step (governed by `transaction`) between `assignHousehold` and `assignCode`.\n\n3. **Owner entity** \u2014 added a persisted `Integer namesakeCount` field (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) with getter/setter, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it.\n\n4. **OpenAPI schema** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema; the generated `OwnerDto` and MapStruct `OwnerMapper` pick it up automatically by name.\n\n5. **DB schema** \u2014 added a `namesake_count` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres), and added the extra `NULL` value to the hsqldb `data.sql` positional seed inserts (the only ones without an explicit column list).\n\nThe `Cp13Tests.coreCountsNamesakes` test and the full 22-test suite are green.",
